.TH "ngspicetclbridge" 3tcl 0\&.5 "ngspicetclbridge" "Tcl NgspiceTclBridge package"
.SH NAME
ngspicetclbridge - Commands in namespace ngspicetclbridge
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBconfigure\fP \fI?option?\fP
.br
\fBconfigure\fP \fI?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
\fBgetCircuit\fP \fI?-logical|-physical|-deck|-expand|-runnable|-param? sim\fP
.br
\fBgetCircuitTitle\fP \fIsim\fP
.br
\fBgetPlotDate\fP \fIsim\fP
.br
\fBgetPlotName\fP \fIsim\fP
.br
\fBgetScaleInfo\fP \fIsim\fP
.br
\fBnew\fP \fI?-nospinit|-nospiceinit|-noinit? libpath ?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-namespace name?\fP
.br
\fBreadVecsAsync\fP \fI?-info? ?-output list|vector? ?-namespace name? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-names dictionary|#auto? sim\fP
.br
\fBrun\fP \fI?-nocleanup? sim\fP
.br
\fBSIM\fP \fIsubcommand \&.\&.\&.\fP
.br
\fBSIM abort\fP \fI?-help?\fP
.br
\fBSIM asyncvector\fP \fIname ?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-name vectorName? ?-namespace name?\fP
.br
\fBSIM asyncvector\fP \fI-info name\fP
.br
\fBSIM circuit\fP \fI?-string? circuit\fP
.br
\fBSIM command\fP \fI?-capture? string\fP
.br
\fBSIM command\fP \fI-clear\fP
.br
\fBSIM destroy\fP \fI?-help?\fP
.br
\fBSIM eventcounts\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
\fBSIM eventdata\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
\fBSIM eventnodes\fP \fI?-all|-nodes names? ?-mode changes|snapshot|pernode?\fP
.br
\fBSIM flush\fP \fI?-help?\fP
.br
\fBSIM initvectors\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
\fBSIM inputpath\fP \fI-current\fP
.br
\fBSIM inputpath\fP \fIpath\fP
.br
\fBSIM isrunning\fP \fI?-help?\fP
.br
\fBSIM messages\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
\fBSIM plot\fP \fI?-all?\fP
.br
\fBSIM plot\fP \fI-vecs name\fP
.br
\fBSIM vectors\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
\fBSIM waitevent\fP \fIname ?-n N? ?-since count? ?timeout_ms?\fP
.br
.SH ::NGSPICETCLBRIDGE
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBconfigure\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Queries or changes package-wide representation and collision defaults in this Tcl interpreter\&.
.RS 4n
\fBconfigure\fP \fI?option?\fP
.br
\fBconfigure\fP \fI?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-ifexists policy
Default destination collision policy: error or replace; initially error\&.
.TP
-output mode
Default output representation: list or vector; initially list\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
With no arguments, returns all settings as an option/value dictionary\&. With one option, returns its value\&.
With option/value pairs, validates all settings before applying them and returns the complete configuration\&.
Invalid options or values, or unavailable RBC support leave the configuration unchanged\&. Selecting
vector mode requires an RBC-enabled build and a loadable rbc::vector package; list queries/settings do not
load RBC\&. Defaults are independent in separate interpreters\&.
.PP
New simulator handles capture these defaults unless -output or -ifexists is supplied explicitly at creation\&.
Existing handles retain their settings\&. Per-read overrides take precedence over the handle default\&.
This public command is not namespace-exported; call it as ::ngspicetclbridge::configure\&.
The collision policy affects vector output only; it can be configured while using list mode or without RBC\&.
Replacement still requires a compatible, writable destination\&. Namespace selection and naming are unchanged\&.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
set saved [::ngspicetclbridge::configure]
::ngspicetclbridge::configure -output vector -ifexists replace
::ngspicetclbridge::configure -output
::ngspicetclbridge::configure {*}$saved
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
selected option value for a single-option query; otherwise all settings as a dictionary\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBgetCircuit\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets list with currently loaded circuit (its listing) in the form specified by the switch\&.
.RS 4n
\fBgetCircuit\fP \fI?-logical|-physical|-deck|-expand|-runnable|-param? sim\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-deck
Just like the physical listing, except without the line numbers it recreates the input file verbatim (except that it does not preserve case)
.TP
-expand
The circuit is printed with all subcircuits expanded\&.
.TP
-logical
The circuit is with all continuation lines collapsed into one line\&.
.TP
-param
Printing all parameters and their actual values\&.
.TP
-physical
The circuits lines are printed out as they were found in the file\&.
.TP
-runnable
Circuit netlist expanded, but without additional line numbers, ready to be sourced again and run in ngspice\&. Default version if no witch is provided\&.
.TP
sim
Simulator handler that is returned by ngspicetclbridge::new
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
list with listing lines
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBgetCircuitTitle\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets title of the current circuit (first line of circuits netlist)\&.
.RS 4n
\fBgetCircuitTitle\fP \fIsim\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
title
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBgetPlotDate\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets time stamp of current plot generation\&.
.RS 4n
\fBgetPlotDate\fP \fIsim\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
time stamp
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBgetPlotName\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets name of the current plot, i\&.e\&. Operating Point, AC Analysis, etc\&.
.RS 4n
\fBgetPlotName\fP \fIsim\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
name of the plot
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBgetScaleInfo\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets dictionary with information about current scale vector\&.
.RS 4n
\fBgetScaleInfo\fP \fIsim\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
dictionary with the information
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBnew\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Load dynamic library, path should be provided in native form for target OS\&.  Every ::ngspicetclbridge::new
returns a command (e\&.g\&. ::ngspicetclbridge::s1)\&. The following subcommands operate on that instance\&.
Optionally the spinit and/or spiceinit initialization files could be forbidden for loading\&.
.RS 4n
\fBnew\fP \fI?-nospinit|-nospiceinit|-noinit? libpath ?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-namespace name?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-ifexists
Error or replace for initial vector destinations; inherits the package configuration (initially error)
.TP
-namespace
Destination for live vectors and snapshots; created at handle construction if missing\&.
.TP
-noinit
Inhibit both spinit and spiceinit\&.
.TP
-nospiceinit
Inhibits spiceinit\&.
.TP
-nospinit
Inhibits spinit\&.
.TP
-output
List or vector; inherits the package configuration (initially list); controls live storage and snapshots\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Namespace:
.TP
\(bu
Relative names resolve against the handle creation caller; the fully qualified name is retained\&.
.TP
\(bu
Missing namespaces and parents are created\&. Empty names are rejected\&.
.TP
\(bu
Destroying the handle does not delete the namespace\&.
.TP
\(bu
Without this option, live vectors use the creation namespace; snapshots use their caller's namespace\&.
.TP
\(bu
Use a dedicated namespace to avoid collisions, such as the signal time and Tcl's global time command\&.
.PP
Vector output:
.TP
\(bu
Requires an RBC-enabled build and rbc::vector with literal-name support\&.
.TP
\(bu
With replace, existing same-type vectors are adopted, preserving their commands and graph clients\&.
.TP
\(bu
Unrelated commands and vectors maintained by another simulator cannot be replaced\&.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
set sim [::ngspicetclbridge::new /usr/local/lib/libngspice\&.so]
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
command name to work with Ngspice instance, references as SIM later
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBreadVecsAsync\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Reads all available vectors of the current plot as independent snapshots\&. Returns a dictionary with
raw vector names as keys and lists or fully qualified RBC vector names as values\&.
.RS 4n
\fBreadVecsAsync\fP \fI?-info? ?-output list|vector? ?-namespace name? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-names dictionary|#auto? sim\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-ifexists
Error or replace; overrides the simulator collision policy\&.
.TP
-info
Return vector metadata instead of data; cannot be combined with output options\&.
.TP
-names
#auto for fresh vectors, or a dictionary of signal names to explicit destinations or #auto
.TP
-namespace
Destination namespace for vector snapshots; created if missing, relative to the caller\&.
.TP
-output
List or vector; overrides the simulator default\&.
.TP
sim
Simulator handle that is returned by ngspicetclbridge::new
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Output and ownership:
.TP
\(bu
Handle defaults apply unless overridden\&. Without an explicit namespace, snapshots use the caller's namespace\&.
.TP
\(bu
Complex data produces complex RBC vectors\&. Snapshots survive simulator destruction\&.
.PP
Naming:
.TP
\(bu
Naming options require vector output\&. RBC generates returned names in the selected namespace\&.
.TP
\(bu
Signals omitted from -names keep signal-derived names\&.
.TP
\(bu
#auto requests automatic naming; auto without # is an ordinary name\&.
.PP
Consistency and errors:
.TP
\(bu
Vectors are copied separately; reading a running simulation is not an atomic snapshot\&.
.TP
\(bu
If a later copy fails, previously created or replaced snapshots remain in the destination namespace\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
dictionary
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBrun\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Runs simulation in a background thread, waits for completion and flushes live data before returning\&.
Does not service the Tcl event loop; GUI events and redraws remain pending\&.
.RS 4n
\fBrun\fP \fI?-nocleanup? sim\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
-nocleanup
If provided, previous ngspice plots are retained; live storage still resets for a new plot\&.
.TP
sim
Simulator handle that is returned by ngspicetclbridge::new
.RE
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
A
command
ensemble\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM\fP \fIsubcommand \&.\&.\&.\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
The ensemble supports the following subcommands:
.RS 4n
.TP
\fIabort\fP
Sets an internal abort flag and wake any waiters (useful to force waitevent to return)\&. This does \fBnot\fP free the instance\&.
.TP
\fIasyncvector\fP
Fetches the current values of a named vector through ngspice's ngGet_Vec_Info\&. Available once the simulation has produced data; the vector may still be incomplete\&.
.TP
\fIcircuit\fP
Sends an circuit to Ngspice in form of the Tcl list, each element is the line of the netlist\&. If switch -string is provided, the input netlists could be passed as ordinary string with newline character as a separator between netlists lines\&.
.TP
\fIcommand\fP
Sends an arbitrary Ngspice command line (e\&.g\&., bg_run, circbyline \&.\&.\&., \&.save, \&.tran, \&.dc)\&. If we provide -capture switch, it returns not only the result code, but also the next message from stdout of Ngspice\&. Also, if command is send in the moment background thread is starting or stopping, it will be deferred to the time is could be safely sent, and in that case -capture message and command results code are not availaible as a return of command\&.
.TP
\fIdestroy\fP
Deletes the instance command\&. In details:
.TP
\fIeventcounts\fP
Raw event counters: send_raw_evt counts native callbacks (including retained disabled registrations); event_init counts event-store initialization on configuration or a new plot; event_batch counts completed raw batches, including batches without changed selected nodes\&. The latter two are bridge-generated events\&. They support waitevent -since and eventcounts -clear just like the existing callback counters\&. Gets or reset the cumulative event counters for this simulator instance\&.
.TP
\fIeventdata\fP
Reads an independent snapshot of published string-valued event data\&.
.TP
\fIeventnodes\fP
Discovers event nodes and selects raw event collection independently of numeric output mode\&.
.TP
\fIflush\fP
Publishes pending initialization metadata and samples for this simulator into live storage\&. Works in both list and vector modes\&. Returns an empty result on success\&.
.TP
\fIinitvectors\fP
Gets held \fBinitial vector metadata\fP (built from send_init_data) in a dict\&.
.TP
\fIinputpath\fP
Gets current path for XSPICE code models if -current switch is provided, or set current path to value provided\&.
.TP
\fIisrunning\fP
Calls asynchronously to check if background thread is running\&.
.TP
\fImessages\fP
Queues of textual messages captured from Ngspice (stdout/stderr) and bridge status lines\&.
.TP
\fIplot\fP
Gets current plot name if no arguments provided, names of all plots or all vectors names that belongs to name of the provided plot\&.
.TP
\fIvectors\fP
Gets data accumulated from send_data events through the Tcl event loop\&.
.TP
\fIwaitevent\fP
Blocks until a named event is observed n number of times (or once), the instance is aborted/destroyed, or the timeout expires (if provided)\&.
.RE
.PP
Refer to the documentation of each subcommand for details\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM abort\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Sets an internal abort flag and wake any waiters (useful to force waitevent to return)\&. This does \fBnot\fP free
the instance\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM abort\fP \fI?-help?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP abort\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
nothing\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM asyncvector\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Fetches the current values of a named vector through ngspice's ngGet_Vec_Info\&. Available once the simulation
has produced data; the vector may still be incomplete\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM asyncvector\fP \fIname ?-output list|vector? ?-ifexists error|replace? ?-name vectorName? ?-namespace name?\fP
.br
\fBSIM asyncvector\fP \fI-info name\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.TP
-ifexists
Error or replace; overrides the handle collision policy\&.
.TP
-info
Returns a metadata dictionary: signal type, real/complex type and length\&.
.TP
-name
Destination name or #auto for a fresh RBC name (vector output only)
.TP
-namespace
Destination namespace; created with missing parents (vector output only)
.TP
-output
List or vector; overrides the handle default for this snapshot\&.
.TP
name
Ngspice vector name\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Ownership and replacement:
.TP
\(bu
Vector output creates an independent, caller-owned snapshot that survives handle destruction\&.
.TP
\(bu
With -ifexists replace, existing same-type snapshot vectors are updated in place\&. Unrelated commands and live vectors maintained by any simulator cannot be overwritten\&.
.PP
Destination namespace:
.TP
\(bu
Uses the explicit handle -namespace, or otherwise the caller's namespace\&.
.TP
\(bu
A per-call -namespace overrides this selection and resolves relative to the caller\&. It does not change handle defaults or live bindings\&. Empty names are rejected\&.
.TP
\(bu
A fully qualified -name overrides the selected namespace; its parent must already exist\&.
.TP
\(bu
#auto creates a fresh RBC vector in the selected namespace\&.
.PP
Signal-derived names and access:
.TP
\(bu
Balanced parentheses, including v(1), remain literal\&. Names unsafe for RBC or containing namespace separators are encoded as _raw_ followed by uppercase hexadecimal UTF-8 bytes\&.
.TP
\(bu
No mapped array variable is created\&. Read values through the vector command, for example: \fI$vector\fP range 0 end\&.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$sim initvectors
$sim asyncvector out
# -> {0\&.0 0\&.066666\&.\&.\&. 0\&.133333\&.\&.\&. \&.\&.\&.}

$sim asyncvector V(9)
# -> {{0\&.01 0\&.00} {0\&.02 0\&.00} \&.\&.\&.}   ;# if complex
.fi
.RE
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP asyncvector\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
real vectors as a flat list of doubles, complex vectors as a list of {re im} pairs\&. Error if vector
does not exists\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM circuit\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Sends an circuit to Ngspice in form of the Tcl list, each element is the line of the netlist\&. If switch
-string is provided, the input netlists could be passed as ordinary string with newline character as a
separator between netlists lines\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM circuit\fP \fI?-string? circuit\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.TP
-string
Allows to pass circuit as ordinary string\&.
.TP
circuit
List of string\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
set resDivCircuit {
    Resistor divider
    v1 in 0 1
    r1 in out 1e3
    r2 out 0 2e3
    \&.dc v1 0 5 0\&.1
    \&.save all
    \&.end
}
$sim circuit [split $resDivCircuit \\n]
$sim command bg_run
.fi
.RE
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP circuit\&.
.PP
Loading a replacement requires an idle simulator\&. The old circuit is removed before loading the new one; a load
failure does not restore it\&. Raw event histories and explicit node selections are cleared\&. The event mode and -all
selection are retained, with -all resolved against the new circuit before this call returns\&.  If automatic event
registration fails, the new circuit remains loaded and this command reports an error\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Ngspice result code
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM command\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Sends an arbitrary Ngspice command line (e\&.g\&., bg_run, circbyline \&.\&.\&., \&.save, \&.tran, \&.dc)\&. If we provide
-capture switch, it returns not only the result code, but also the next message from stdout of Ngspice\&. Also, if
command is send in the moment background thread is starting or stopping, it will be deferred to the time is could
be safely sent, and in that case -capture message and command results code are not availaible as a return of
command\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM command\fP \fI?-capture? string\fP
.br
\fBSIM command\fP \fI-clear\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.TP
-capture
Return captured output along with the result code\&.
.TP
-clear
Release retained ngspice command memory at an idle boundary\&.
.TP
string
Command string; omitted with -clear\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Command memory:
.TP
\(bu
command -clear calls ngSpice_Command(NULL) and returns its result code\&. An empty string does not do this\&.
.TP
\(bu
Use a handle created with -noinit (or both -nospinit and -nospiceinit), driven directly from Tcl\&.
.TP
\(bu
Cleanup is rejected during background startup, execution or shutdown, native calls, and pending commands\&. It never halts a simulation or defers cleanup\&. After bg_halt returns, cleanup permits a later bg_resume\&.
.TP
\(bu
Scripts, aliases, includes and control workers disable cleanup permanently for that handle\&. Detection is conservative, including matching text in comments\&. Initialization files also disable cleanup because ngspice exposes no reliable query/join for its separate control worker\&.
.TP
\(bu
Cleanup discards command history, labels and unfinished control blocks\&. Only call it between complete command sequences\&. It preserves circuit state, plots, snapshots, live vectors/lists and bridge messages\&.
.TP
\(bu
Unlike destroy all, vectors -clear and messages -clear, this releases the command interpreter's storage\&. The run helper does not do this automatically, so existing control-script behavior remains unchanged\&.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$sim command {circbyline v1 in 0 1}
$sim command bg_run
.fi
.RE
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP command\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
Ngspice result code, or dictionary with result code and the message
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM destroy\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Deletes the instance command\&. In details:
.RS 4n
\fBSIM destroy\fP \fI?-help?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.TP
\(bu
Marks the context as destroying
.TP
\(bu
Wakes any waiters
.TP
\(bu
Quiesces the ngspice background thread
.TP
\(bu
Defers and performs full cleanup
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP destroy\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
nothing\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM eventcounts\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Raw event counters: send_raw_evt counts native callbacks (including retained disabled registrations);
event_init counts event-store initialization on configuration or a new plot; event_batch counts completed
raw batches, including batches without changed selected nodes\&. The latter two are bridge-generated events\&.
They support waitevent -since and eventcounts -clear just like the existing callback counters\&.
Gets or reset the cumulative event counters for this simulator instance\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM eventcounts\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.TP
-clear
Zeros all counts and returns nothing\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$sim eventcounts
# -> send_char N  send_stat N  controlled_exit N send_data N  send_init_data N  bg_running N
.fi
.RE
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP eventcounts\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
returns a dict with keys as events names, and counts for each event as a value
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM eventdata\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Reads an independent snapshot of published string-valued event data\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM eventdata\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.TP
-clear
Discard stored and pending event history; retain selection and latest known states\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Result keys are mode, generation, nodes and batches\&. nodes maps names to dictionaries containing type\&.
In pernode mode each node also has events: a list of {eventTime stringValue last} records\&.
In changes mode batches contains {time sampleTime events {{node eventTime stringValue last} \&.\&.\&.}} dictionaries\&.
In snapshot mode batches contains {time sampleTime values {node stringValue \&.\&.\&.} known {node \&.\&.\&.}} dictionaries\&.
An uninitialized node has an empty value and is absent from known; this differs from ngspice's explicit U state\&.
last is only the end of ONE node's native batch, never an all-nodes completion marker\&. Event times can be
out of order across nodes; callback order and repeated same-time transitions are preserved\&.
.PP
Data is copied from mutex-protected C storage on this call; no Tcl event-loop turn is required\&. A read or flush
cannot complete a partially delivered timestep\&. Clear does not erase ngspice's own saved event data or reset
counters; later callbacks continue recording\&. A fresh plot clears histories; halt/resume preserves them\&.  Decoder
errors are retained and returned here until a new plot or configuration resets them\&.  Numeric
-output/-namespace/-ifexists settings do not apply; event values are always Tcl strings\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
dictionary of published event data\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM eventnodes\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Discovers event nodes and selects raw event collection independently of numeric output mode\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM eventnodes\fP \fI?-all|-nodes names? ?-mode changes|snapshot|pernode?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.TP
-all
Select all names returned by ngSpice_AllEvtNodes, including internal subcircuit nodes\&.
.TP
-mode mode
Changes, snapshot or pernode; initially changes\&.
.TP
-nodes names
Select an explicit list; an empty list disables recording\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Call after loading the circuit and while idle, before run/bg_run\&. Without options, returns supported, available,
selected and mode\&. Raw symbols are optional; unsupported libraries retain analog functionality\&.  Each node is
registered once per loaded circuit\&. Changing selection or mode clears event history and known states\&.  Resume
retains registrations and histories\&. Disabled registrations remain alive until circuit replacement or handle
destruction\&.  Event collection supports externally driven transient analyses\&. After registering nodes, use the
circuit subcommand to replace the circuit while idle\&. Mode and -all are retained; explicit -nodes selections,
known states and histories are cleared\&. Direct source/reset/remcirc/setcirc/circbyline commands and
circuit-changing scripts or aliases remain unsupported\&.
.PP
All modes collect through SendRawEvtData and preserve ngspice's printable strings, including drive strength\&.
changes publishes complete accepted-step batches; snapshot publishes every selected node at accepted analog
output times, carrying unchanged values forward; pernode exposes individual events immediately\&.
Complete batches become visible at the next analog output callback, or after completion/halt for the final
batch\&. Pure digital transient circuits use ngspice's time-only output\&. There is no wall-clock sampling timer\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
dictionary describing support, available nodes, selected nodes and mode\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM flush\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Publishes pending initialization metadata and samples for this simulator into live storage\&.
Works in both list and vector modes\&. Returns an empty result on success\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM flush\fP \fI?-help?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
The command processes one buffered batch without waiting for simulation completion or servicing the Tcl
event loop\&. Samples arriving during publication remain pending for a later flush or event-loop iteration\&.
Initialization is applied before samples\&. Repeated calls without new data have no effect, and queued
bridge events cannot append the same samples twice\&. Existing notifications for this handle are removed
before publication so repeated flushes do not retain an unbounded event queue\&. Callback counters are unchanged\&.
.PP
Publication errors are returned directly and retained for subsequent flush/vectors calls until a new plot\&.
RBC notifications may invoke application callbacks\&. Reentrant operations on this handle are rejected
during publication, except destruction\&. Graph redraws still require normal Tk event processing\&.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$sim command run
$sim flush
set data [$sim vectors]
.fi
.RE
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP flush\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
empty string
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM initvectors\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets held \fBinitial vector metadata\fP (built from send_init_data) in a dict\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM initvectors\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.TP
-clear
Empties the internal memory structure and returns \fBnothing\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$sim initvectors
# -> out {number 1 real 1} in {number 2 real 1} v-sweep {number 3 real 1}
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBWarning\fP: accumulation of data \fBdo not\fP continues after call bg_run, new metadata replace the old one
in the storage\&.
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP initvectors\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
dict with initial vector metadata saved in internal structure
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM inputpath\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets current path for XSPICE code models if -current switch is provided, or set current path to value
provided\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM inputpath\fP \fI-current\fP
.br
\fBSIM inputpath\fP \fIpath\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.TP
-current
Switch to return current path\&.
.TP
path
Full path to desired location\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP inputpath\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
current path
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM isrunning\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Calls asynchronously to check if background thread is running\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM isrunning\fP \fI?-help?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP isrunning\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
1 if thread is running, 0 otherwise\&.
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM messages\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Queues of textual messages captured from Ngspice (stdout/stderr) and bridge status lines\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM messages\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.TP
-clear
Empties the internal queue structure and returns \fBnothing\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
join [$sim messages] \\n
# stdout ******
# stdout ** ngspice-44\&.x shared library
# \&.\&.\&.
# # status[0]: --ready--
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBWarning\fP: accumulation of messages continues even if you run new circuit or analysis until you explicitly
clear the data storage\&.
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP messages\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
list of messages
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM plot\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets current plot name if no arguments provided, names of all plots or all vectors names that belongs to
name of the provided plot\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM plot\fP \fI?-all?\fP
.br
\fBSIM plot\fP \fI-vecs name\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.TP
-all
Switch to return all plots names\&.
.TP
-vecs plotname
Switch with argument to get all vectors names belonging to name plot\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP plot\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
current plot, or list of all plots, or list of all vectors
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM vectors\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Gets data accumulated from send_data events through the Tcl event loop\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM vectors\fP \fI?-clear?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.TP
-clear
Empties stored samples and returns \fBnothing\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
Output:
.TP
\(bu
List mode: dictionary mapping signal names to lists\&. Complex samples use interleaved real/imaginary doubles\&.
.TP
\(bu
Vector mode: dictionary mapping raw signal names to fully qualified live RBC vector commands\&. Real and complex signals use the corresponding vector types\&.
.PP
Updates and clearing:
.TP
\(bu
Each new plot replaces stored list data, for both run and bg_run\&. Lists contain the current plot's accumulated samples, not concatenated history\&. Previously returned dictionaries remain valid\&.
.TP
\(bu
Halting preserves samples\&. Resuming the same plot appends to them, including samples still queued for Tcl processing\&. A different plot resets storage even when reached through resume\&.
.TP
\(bu
Explicit -clear empties stored samples and discards already queued samples in both output modes\&. Samples received afterwards continue appending; ngspice snapshot data is unaffected\&.
.TP
\(bu
Vector identities remain stable across runs\&. Each new plot clears retained vectors, including signals absent from that plot\&.
.TP
\(bu
Updates require Tcl event processing or an explicit flush; eventcounts/waitevent alone do not publish queued samples\&. The run helper flushes automatically before returning\&.
.TP
\(bu
In vector mode, -clear preserves vector commands and their graph bindings\&.
.PP
Ownership and renaming:
.TP
\(bu
The handle destroys vectors it created; adopted vectors remain alive\&.
.TP
\(bu
Treat live contents as read-only\&. Deleting, resizing or replacing attached vectors invalidates continued streaming\&.
.TP
\(bu
Use rbc::vector rename oldName newName to rename a live vector\&. Its identity, ownership and streaming connection are preserved across clear and subsequent runs\&.
.TP
\(bu
After renaming completes, query the bridge for the updated dictionary: signal keys remain unchanged, while destination names reflect the rename\&.
.TP
\(bu
Ordinary Tcl rename is unsupported because it leaves RBC's registry unchanged\&.
.PP
Errors:
.TP
\(bu
Asynchronous output failures are reported once through Tcl's background error handler and on subsequent vectors calls\&. Incoming samples are discarded until a new plot initializes output\&.
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$sim vectors
# -> v(out) {0\&.0 0\&.1 0\&.2 \&.\&.\&.} v(in) {\&.\&.\&.} v-sweep {\&.\&.\&.}

$sim vectors -clear
# -> (no result; succeeds)
.fi
.RE
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP vectors\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
dict with vectors values accumulated up to this point in internal structure
.PP
.RS -4n
\fBSIM waitevent\fR (::ngspicetclbridge)
.RE
.PP
Blocks until a named event is observed n number of times (or once), the instance is aborted/destroyed,
or the timeout expires (if provided)\&.
.RS 4n
\fBSIM waitevent\fP \fIname ?-n N? ?-since count? ?timeout_ms?\fP
.br
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fR
.RS 4n
.TP
handle
Not documented\&.
.TP
-n N
Required number of callbacks relative to the baseline; defaults to one\&.
.TP
-since count
Optional baseline captured with eventcounts before starting the operation\&.
.TP
name
Name of the event\&.
.TP
timeout_ms
Timeout in miliseconds, optional\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDescription\fR
.PP
.nf
┌─────────────────┬──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Event name      │ Ngspice callback         │ When it is called                                                       │
│                 │ function name            │                                                                         │
├─────────────────┼──────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ send_char       │ SendChar                 │ Whenever Ngspice produces a line of text on stdout or stderr\&.           │
│ send_stat       │ SendStat                 │ When Ngspice’s simulation status changes (e\&.g\&., --ready--, tran 50\&.1%,  │
│                 │                          │ convergence messages)\&.                                                  │
│ controlled_exit │ ControlledExit           │ When Ngspice exits, either due to an error or after a quit command from │
│                 │                          │ Tcl/Ngspice\&.                                                            │
│ send_data       │ SendData                 │ During an analysis, whenever Ngspice sends a row of vector values (time │
│                 │                          │ step or sweep point) to the callback\&.                                   │
│ send_init_data  │ SendInitData             │ At the start of a run, when Ngspice sends metadata for all vectors in   │
│                 │                          │ the current plot (names, types, indexes, real/complex)\&.                 │
│ bg_running      │ BGThreadRunning          │ When the Ngspice background thread changes state: running=false means   │
│                 │                          │ it just started running, running=true means it has stopped\&.             │
└─────────────────┴──────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

.fi
.PP
.nf
┌──────┬─────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────┬─────────────────────┐
│ Time │ Tcl Script Action       │ Ngspice Core Activity       │ Bridge Callback Fired  │ Tcl Event Name Seen │
├──────┼─────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────┼─────────────────────┤
│ t0   │ set s [\&.\&.::new \&.\&.]      │ Library loaded              │ (none)                 │ (none)              │
│ t1   │ $s init                 │ Initialization completed    │ (none)                 │ (none)              │
│ t2   │ cirPass …               │ Parses circuit line         │ send_char("\&.\&.\&.")       │ send_char           │
│ t3   │ (more circbyline calls) │ Parses circuit line         │ send_char("\&.\&.\&.")       │ send_char           │
│ t4   │ $s command bg_run       │ Start background simulation │ bg_running(false)      │ bg_running          │
│ t5   │ (analysis setup)        │ Build vector table          │ send_init_data()       │ send_init_data      │
│ t6   │ (analysis running)      │ First data point            │ send_data(\&.\&.\&.)         │ send_data           │
│ t7   │ (analysis running)      │ More points                 │ send_data(\&.\&.\&.)         │ send_data           │
│ t8   │ (analysis running)      │ Status change               │ send_stat("\&.\&.\&.")       │ send_stat           │
│ t9   │ (analysis completed)    │ Simulation ready            │ send_stat("--ready--") │ send_stat           │
│ t10  │ (BG thread exits)       │ Background thread exits     │ bg_running(true)       │ bg_running          │
│ t11  │ $s command quit         │ ngspice quits               │ controlled_exit(\&.\&.\&.)   │ controlled_exit     │
│ t12  │ $s destroy              │ Teardown                    │ (no further calls)     │ (command removed)   │
└──────┴─────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────┴─────────────────────┘

.fi
.PP
Result dictionary of the command:
.TP
\(bu
fired - 0|1, whether the target count was reached
.TP
\(bu
count - cumulative total count for that event so far
.TP
\(bu
status - ok | timeout | aborted
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
$sim waitevent send_stat 1000
# -> {fired 1 count 1 status ok}

$sim waitevent send_stat 1000
# -> {fired 0 count 1 status timeout}  ;# nothing new in the next 1s
.fi
.RE
.PP
By default, only callbacks received after entering the wait count\&. To include callbacks received
between starting an operation and waiting, capture a baseline first:
.PP
.RS 4n
.nf
set baseline [dict get [$sim eventcounts] bg_running]
$sim command bg_run
$sim waitevent bg_running -since $baseline -n 2 10000
.fi
.RE
.PP
With -since, the target is baseline + N; an already reached target returns immediately\&.
Use a count from the same handle and event\&. Do not clear counters between capturing it and waiting\&.
A timeout returns status timeout, not a Tcl error\&. This command does not process queued data updates\&.
.PP
The handle argument is supplied automatically when called as \fI$handle\fP waitevent\&.
.PP
\fBReturn value\fR
.PP
dictionary with information about event


